  "definition": "A control moment gyroscope (CMG) is a spacecraft torque actuator that steers the angular-momentum vector of a spinning rotor. Its rotor normally keeps a large, approximately constant spin momentum while a motor rotates the rotor assembly about one or more gimbal axes. The spacecraft experiences the opposing torque associated with the change in that momentum vector.[^nasa-actuators-2024]",
